<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><?xml-stylesheet href="/pretty-feed-v3.xsl" type="text/xsl"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Symbian C++ on Hugo van Kemenade</title><link>https://hugovk.dev/tags/symbian-c++/</link><description>Recent content in Symbian C++ on Hugo van Kemenade</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><copyright>&lt;a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"&gt;{{&lt; icon "cc" &gt;}}&amp;hairsp;{{&lt; icon "cc-by" &gt;}}&amp;hairsp;{{&lt; icon "cc-sa" &gt;}}&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;Hugo van Kemenade&lt;br&gt;&lt;p class="text-xs text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400"&gt;Powered by &lt;a class="hover:underline hover:decoration-primary-400 hover:text-primary-500" href="https://gohugo.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Hugo&lt;/a&gt; &amp;amp; &lt;a class="hover:underline hover:decoration-primary-400 hover:text-primary-500" href="https://github.com/jpanther/congo" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Congo&lt;/a&gt; &amp;amp; &lt;a class="hover:underline hover:decoration-primary-400 hover:text-primary-500" href="https://hugovk.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Hugo&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</copyright><lastBuildDate>Mon, 08 Apr 2013 17:27:06 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://hugovk.dev/tags/symbian-c++/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Symbian platform share in the Ovi Store (IV)</title><link>https://hugovk.dev/blog/2013/symbian-platform-share-iv/</link><pubDate>Mon, 08 Apr 2013 17:27:06 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://hugovk.dev/blog/2013/symbian-platform-share-iv/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20130429152255/http://www.developer.nokia.com/Community/Blogs/code.google.com/p/mobbler/"&gt;Mobbler&lt;/a&gt;,&#10;the open-source&#10;&lt;a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20130429111842/http://www.last.fm/group/Mobbler&amp;#43;Users"&gt;Last.fm&lt;/a&gt;&#10;radio player and scrobbler for Symbian smartphones is five years old today!&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;To commemorate, here&amp;rsquo;s an updated (generated by&#10;&lt;a href="../../2011/symbian-platform-share"&gt;Ovid&lt;/a&gt;) chart showing the share of its 225,098&#10;downloads in the&#10;&lt;a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20130429152255/http://store.ovi.com/content/75692"&gt;Nokia Store&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/hugovk/8630568841/"&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;figure&gt;&#10; &#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10; &lt;picture&#10; class="mx-auto my-0 rounded-md"&#10; &#10; &gt;&#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &lt;source&#10; &#10; srcset="https://hugovk.dev/blog/2013/symbian-platform-share-iv/ovid-mobbler-2013-04_hu_1e2709c2a60d274a.webp 330w,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2013/symbian-platform-share-iv/ovid-mobbler-2013-04_hu_b7e1e98ab2a7fcf.webp 660w&#10; &#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2013/symbian-platform-share-iv/ovid-mobbler-2013-04_hu_54014919f8e17ac3.webp 1024w&#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2013/symbian-platform-share-iv/ovid-mobbler-2013-04_hu_54014919f8e17ac3.webp 1024w&#10; &#10; "&#10; &#10; sizes="100vw"&#10; type="image/webp"&#10; /&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;img&#10; width="1024"&#10; height="600"&#10; class="mx-auto my-0 rounded-md"&#10; alt="Mobbler downloads from Nokia Store (21st Feb 2011 - 8th April 2013) by hugovk, on Flickr"&#10; loading="lazy" decoding="async"&#10; &#10; src="https://hugovk.dev/blog/2013/symbian-platform-share-iv/ovid-mobbler-2013-04_hu_446bddc8a23829e5.png" srcset="https://hugovk.dev/blog/2013/symbian-platform-share-iv/ovid-mobbler-2013-04_hu_f3e456ab112bbef5.png 330w,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2013/symbian-platform-share-iv/ovid-mobbler-2013-04_hu_446bddc8a23829e5.png 660w&#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2013/symbian-platform-share-iv/ovid-mobbler-2013-04.png 1024w&#10; &#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2013/symbian-platform-share-iv/ovid-mobbler-2013-04.png 1024w&#10; "&#10; sizes="100vw"&#10; &#10; /&gt;&#10; &lt;/picture&gt;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;With a second year&amp;rsquo;s worth of download data, it&amp;rsquo;s interesting to see S60 3rd Edition is&#10;still going strong.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Figures for the last full month (March 2013):&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;==============================&#10;11 Symbian Belle models: 28.7%&#10;3 Symbian Anna models: 1.1%&#10;5 Symbian^3 models: 4.6%&#10;12 Symbian^1 models: 30.5%&#10;38 S60 3rd ed. models: 36%&#10;------------------------------&#10;22 S60 3.2 models: 17.5%&#10;12 S60 3.1 models: 14.9%&#10;4 S60 3.0 models: 3.1%&#10;==============================&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href="../../2011/symbian-platform-share-ii"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; for some older charts for other&#10;applications. Let me know if you create charts for your applications.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Originally posted on&#10;&lt;a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20130429152255/https://www.developer.nokia.com/Community/Blogs/blog/hugo-van-kemenades-forum-nokia-blog/2013/04/08/symbian-platform-share-in-the-ovi-store-iv"&gt;Hugo van Kemenade&amp;rsquo;s Forum Nokia Blog&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;</description></item><item><title>Symbian platform share in the Nokia Store (III)</title><link>https://hugovk.dev/blog/2012/symbian-platform-share-iii/</link><pubDate>Mon, 12 Mar 2012 21:59:47 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://hugovk.dev/blog/2012/symbian-platform-share-iii/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20120523061840/http://code.google.com/p/mobbler/"&gt;Mobbler&lt;/a&gt;&#10;has now been in the Nokia Store for a year (not counting the previous stint under&#10;Symbian Horizon), so here&amp;rsquo;s an updated chart generated using&#10;&lt;a href="../../2011/symbian-platform-share"&gt;Ovid&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/hugovk/6977065187/"&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;figure&gt;&#10; &#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10; &lt;picture&#10; class="mx-auto my-0 rounded-md"&#10; &#10; &gt;&#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &lt;source&#10; &#10; srcset="https://hugovk.dev/blog/2012/symbian-platform-share-iii/ovid-mobbler-2012-02_hu_7e8b505cf86a93cc.webp 330w,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2012/symbian-platform-share-iii/ovid-mobbler-2012-02_hu_7bac079ebfc0babb.webp 660w&#10; &#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2012/symbian-platform-share-iii/ovid-mobbler-2012-02_hu_c88a046ce5003216.webp 1024w&#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2012/symbian-platform-share-iii/ovid-mobbler-2012-02_hu_c88a046ce5003216.webp 1024w&#10; &#10; "&#10; &#10; sizes="100vw"&#10; type="image/webp"&#10; /&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;img&#10; width="1024"&#10; height="600"&#10; class="mx-auto my-0 rounded-md"&#10; alt="Mobbler downloads from Nokia Store (21st Feb 2011 - 29th Feb 2012) by hugovk, on Flickr"&#10; loading="lazy" decoding="async"&#10; &#10; src="https://hugovk.dev/blog/2012/symbian-platform-share-iii/ovid-mobbler-2012-02_hu_5062e934979b324a.png" srcset="https://hugovk.dev/blog/2012/symbian-platform-share-iii/ovid-mobbler-2012-02_hu_b75a5955f4bec703.png 330w,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2012/symbian-platform-share-iii/ovid-mobbler-2012-02_hu_5062e934979b324a.png 660w&#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2012/symbian-platform-share-iii/ovid-mobbler-2012-02.png 1024w&#10; &#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2012/symbian-platform-share-iii/ovid-mobbler-2012-02.png 1024w&#10; "&#10; sizes="100vw"&#10; &#10; /&gt;&#10; &lt;/picture&gt;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;With a year&amp;rsquo;s worth of download data, it&amp;rsquo;s interesting to see S60 3rd Edition is still&#10;going strong. There&amp;rsquo;s a recent peak in Symbian Belle after I noticed distribution wasn&amp;rsquo;t&#10;set for all Belle devices in the Nokia Store settings.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href="../../2011/symbian-platform-share-ii"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; for some older charts for other&#10;applications. Let me know if you create charts for your applications.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Originally posted on&#10;&lt;a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20120523061840/http://www.developer.nokia.com/Community/Blogs/blog/hugo-van-kemenades-forum-nokia-blog/2012/03/12/symbian-platform-share-in-the-nokia-store-iii"&gt;Hugo van Kemenade&amp;rsquo;s Forum Nokia Blog&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;</description></item></channel></rss>